---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'June 19, 2026';
const description =
  'Simple Fasting privacy policy: local app storage, no account, no tracking, no advertising, and user-controlled export and deletion.';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Simple Fasting" description={description} legal>
  <header class="legal-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="legal-meta">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>
        Simple Fasting is designed so your fasting data can remain on your device. This policy
        explains what the app and this website do—and, just as importantly, what they do not do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="legal-content shell">
    <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
      <a href="#scope">Scope</a>
      <a href="#app-data">App data</a>
      <a href="#permissions">Permissions</a>
      <a href="#controls">Your controls</a>
      <a href="#website">Website privacy</a>
      <a href="#security">Security</a>
      <a href="#children">Children</a>
      <a href="#changes">Changes</a>
      <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <section id="scope">
        <h2>1. Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This policy applies to the Simple Fasting mobile application and the Simple Fasting
          website. The app does not require an account and is intended to work without a custom
          backend or cloud service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="app-data">
        <h2>2. Data in the app</h2>
        <h3>Data you create</h3>
        <p>The app may store the following information locally on your device:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Active and completed fasting sessions, including start and end times.</li>
          <li>Fasting goals and optional reasons you enter.</li>
          <li>Theme, accent, reminder, and widget preferences.</li>
          <li>Locally derived statistics, charts, and heatmaps.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>How it is used</h3>
        <p>
          This data is used on your device to run the timer, build history and statistics, schedule
          local reminders, refresh supported widgets, and create exports you request.
        </p>
        <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
        <p>
          The current app does not use accounts, advertising SDKs, analytics SDKs, cross-app
          tracking, or a Simple Fasting backend. We do not intentionally receive your fasting
          history, reasons, goals, or settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="permissions">
        <h2>3. Device permissions and system features</h2>
        <p>
          If you enable reminders, the app asks the operating system for notification permission.
          Notifications are scheduled locally. Supported widgets, Live Activities, Dynamic Island,
          and Android ongoing notifications are provided through operating-system features and use
          the local fasting state needed to display them.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can change notification permissions in your device settings and app preferences at
          any time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="controls">
        <h2>4. Your data controls</h2>
        <p>You control the data stored by Simple Fasting:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Edit or delete completed fasting sessions.</li>
          <li>Export app data in JSON or CSV format.</li>
          <li>Clear all local app data from Settings.</li>
          <li>Remove app data by uninstalling the app, subject to your device backup settings.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Export files leave the app only when you choose a destination through the system share
          sheet. The privacy practices of that destination then apply.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="website">
        <h2>5. Website privacy</h2>
        <p>
          This website does not intentionally set analytics cookies, run advertising trackers, or
          ask you to create an account. It is delivered as static HTML and CSS.
        </p>
        <p>
          The hosting and network providers used to deliver the site may process ordinary technical
          request information—such as IP address, user agent, timestamps, and requested pages—for
          security, reliability, and delivery. Their own privacy terms govern that processing.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you email support, your email provider and ours process the address, message, and any
          information you choose to include so we can respond.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="security">
        <h2>6. Security and retention</h2>
        <p>
          Local-first design reduces the amount of data transmitted to us, but no device or storage
          system is completely secure. Protect access to your device and choose export destinations
          carefully. Because we do not receive your local app data, we cannot recover it for you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="children">
        <h2>7. Children</h2>
        <p>
          Simple Fasting does not knowingly collect personal information from children. Fasting may
          be inappropriate for some people, including children and adolescents. A parent, guardian,
          or qualified healthcare professional should be consulted before a minor uses a fasting
          tracker.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy when the app, website, or legal requirements change. The updated
          version will appear on this page with a revised effective date. Material changes will not
          silently convert local-only data into remotely collected data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Privacy questions can be sent to
          <a href="mailto:support@simplefasting.app">support@simplefasting.app</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
